| The records (`records`) | Which admitted records support the account? |

The strip's fourth figure is the March commitment of up to 400 million barrels, not the US share of 172. Placing 172 beside 100 invites a sum that is not the event. Three things to know would restate the fold. Who pays is the diesel price and Bessent's sentence inside Where this sits, not a section. The price series are that baseline, not a markets section: they stop before October 2. No outlet error is A or B except the misreadings the catch already carries, so there is no outlets section. The refinery measure is a paragraph of What happened, not its own section.

## Outline

### What happened

- `govuk-g7-statement-2026-10-02`: 100 million barrels over four months, substantial diesel in 20 days, commitments already fulfilled, refinery coordination, Hormuz not restored, no export restrictions among members.
- `elysee-g7-readout-2026-10-02`: up to 100 million barrels of diesel and crude; Hormuz and Yanbu volumes increasing, with no number.
- `iea-contributions-2026-03-19`: March's release largely crude, Europe's share primarily refined products.
- `cnbc-export-ban-2026-09-30`: Wright on diesel tight from lost exports, and American refiners at record highs.
- Gap to admit: `audit-gap-iea-omr-2026-09`, the 390,000 barrels a day and the 1.6 million barrel-a-day shortfall.
- `doe-spr-release-2026-03-11` and `doe-spr-exchange-2026-09-29`: the before-state in one paragraph, March's 400 million and 172 million, more than 133 million already awarded, Europe's fraction, the open exchange of up to 40 million. The rest of those records is Where this sits.

### The catch

- `wsj-g7-release-2026-10-02`: the lede a stranger may have read as a fresh 100 million barrels of crude and fuel.
- `trumpstruth-post-2026-10-02`: a massive immediate release of Europe's diesel.
- `reuters-eu-proposal-2026-10-02`: the 50 million diesel plus 50 million crude proposal, and the demand for 100 million barrels of diesel within 20 days.
- `govuk-g7-statement-2026-10-02` and `elysee-g7-readout-2026-10-02`: fulfilled commitments, substantial rather than a number, and the French ceiling.
- Gap to admit: `audit-gap-iea-oct2-2026-10-02`, around 325 million barrels of the March action already released.
- Gap to admit: `audit-gap-iea-workbook-2026-03-19`, about 426 million barrels of listed contributions, not a second release.

### Where this sits

- `elysee-g7-communique-2026-03-11`: up to 400 million barrels on March 11.
- `iea-contributions-2026-03-19`: the sixth collective action, after 1991, 2005, 2011 and twice in 2022.
- `doe-spr-release-2026-03-11` and `doe-spr-exchange-2026-09-29`: 172 million announced, more than 133 million awarded, up to 40 million still a request.
- `bundesregierung-energy-faq-2026-10-01`: a reserve of about 20 million tonnes, a request for 2.6 million tonnes, and the market not wanting more.
- `gasdesw-2026-10-03`: $6.382 on September 28 and $3.897 on March 2. Brent and WTI stay in the detail of this section.
- `bessent-post-2026-10-01`: farmers, truckers and businesses.
- Gap to admit: `audit-gap-eia-distillate-2026-09-30`, 105.180 million barrels on September 25.
- Gap to admit: `audit-gap-ec-taskforce-2026-10-02`, EU supply stable for the time being.

### The export ban

- `hr10422-diesel-export-2026-09-16`: introduced and referred. H.R. 10423 is the same status, in detail.
- `cnbc-export-ban-2026-09-30`: still thinking about a ban on September 30.
- `bessent-post-2026-10-01`: the October 1 demand that Europe move existing and additional supplies.
- `france24-g7-release-2026-10-02`: the spokeswoman's rejection.
- `govuk-g7-statement-2026-10-02`: no export restrictions between G7 countries.
- `reuters-no-export-ban-2026-10-02`: he will not authorize a diesel export ban.
- `rte-von-der-leyen-2026-10-02`: the Commission president welcomes no export bans on allies. That sentence is the same-day answer; the rest of her post can sit here or in What happened next, once.

### What happened next

- `rte-von-der-leyen-2026-10-02`: the welcome, if it is not already in the export-ban section.
- `govuk-g7-statement-2026-10-02`: a further meeting on diesel, and a report before 20 days. Neither was due on October 3.
- `doe-spr-exchange-2026-09-29`: bids due October 6, and deliveries of already awarded exchanges scheduled for November and December.
- Watching line: the October 6 bids, the report, and any member notice of an actual release.

### What we do not know yet

- `govuk-g7-statement-2026-10-02`: no diesel number and no country shares. The report may address them later. That due date is a next step.
- Gap to admit: `audit-gap-iea-oct2-2026-10-02`. The 325 million figure does not say how much of the October 100 is additional.
- `bundesregierung-energy-faq-2026-10-01`: 2.6 million tonnes is a March request, not an October share.
- `france24-g7-release-2026-10-02`: eighty percent still in pocket is overall stocks.
- `rte-von-der-leyen-2026-10-02`: a same-day drop of as much as 5 percent, which `gasdesw-2026-10-03` does not contain.
- Gap to admit: `audit-gap-october-ledger-2026-10-03`. Search first for an allocation or delivery ledger, a member notice through October 3, and an October 6 award. Do not print this line as the page's unknown.

### The records

- `StorySources` keeps every admitted record. The UK and French English statements are one lineage. Price files are the series, not a second witness to delivery.

